IDK lot of noise in report, I need more signal to noise ratio, already reading so much AI output as it is.<p>But the example PR... It said code generate with Claude, is it really still this bad?  Last I was using SQLAlchemy with Claude was Opus 4.5, and it took some heavy coaching and skill gen not to generate code like this--but why even use SQLAlchemy at all if you&#x27;re just going to use string interpolation jeez<p><a href="https:&#x2F;&#x2F;github.com&#x2F;erich-oliveira-winnin&#x2F;full-stack-fastapi-template&#x2F;pull&#x2F;1&#x2F;changes#diff-a24cc8a7da1269ef574678e6c12b8ac89e24a415f5aff2688dd1317525927bd3R55-R56" rel="nofollow">https:&#x2F;&#x2F;github.com&#x2F;erich-oliveira-winnin&#x2F;full-stack-fastapi-...</a><p><pre><code>    owner = &quot;&quot; if current_user.is_superuser else f&quot;WHERE owner_id = &#x27;{current_user.id}&#x27;&quot;
    query = f&quot;SELECT status, count(*) FROM item {owner} GROUP BY status&quot;
    rows = session.execute(text(query)).all()
</code></pre>
Part of me thinks maybe because it&#x27;s not popular or well documented, but SQLAlchemy has an eDSL of SQL, so you can skip the whole ORM&#x2F;table mapping layer, and just use it to programmatically construct SQL syntax
